{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/800683-luna-eclipse","id":800683,"title":"luna eclipse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-04T12:31:23-08:00","id":800683,"title":"luna eclipse","content":"if a foresakens auspice is affected by the phase of the moon when they have their first change, what would happen if there was a luna eclipse?<br /> <br /> might sound daft but luna eclipses are a real thing and after reading a few of the werewolf books ive not seen this anywhere<br /> <br /> obviously it be supe rare<br /> <br /> if it is in one of the books could someone point me in the right direction? thanks<br /> <br /> if its not in the books what are everyones thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10748-fatninja","name":"fatninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T12:36:54-08:00","id":800688,"title":"","content":"I don't remember which books they're from, but lunar eclipses give you Suharahu (Rahu who emphasize cunning, sometimes known as Trickster Warriors), while solar eclipses give you Hiriraka (Irraka who thrive on chaos and unpredictability).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T12:44:06-08:00","id":800690,"title":"","content":"Signs of the Moon had a section on creating new Auspices, and included a few examples - lunar eclipse, solar eclipse, blood moon, and &quot;stellar eclipse&quot; which I don't think is a real thing. Most of them were just slight variations on an existing Auspice, only swapping out the Auspice ability and sometimes an Auspice Skill or Affinity Gift or two. The stellar eclipse one was the only one with its own Moon Gift.<br /> <br /> The book was also pretty clear that these extra Auspices go against the setting's default assumptions, basically saying there are five Auspices for a reason, but if you want to homebrew more anyway, here are a few examples. So a werewolf who First Changes under a lunar eclipse would be a Rahu by the default setting (since the moon is full during a lunar eclipse, it's just in Earth's shadow), but if you like the idea of them having a different Auspice, check out Signs of the Moon, it has good advice on custom Auspices and an example Lunar Eclipse Auspice. It's First Edition, but a lot of it is still applicable to Second Edition too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T12:53:15-08:00","id":800696,"title":"","content":"cool thanks for the replies ill check out signs of the moon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","sig